I walk past the leather jackets.
One jacket is beautiful.
It is soft, dark brown and exactly my style.
I look for the size.
The brown leather jacket is size thirty-eight.
I already have the green coat over my arm.
I put the coat on a chair.
Then I put the brown jacket on.
I look in the mirror.
The dark jacket fits me perfectly.
I think it is great, because I really like wearing brown.
Then I look at the price tag.
The beautiful jacket costs two hundred and fifty euros.
That is a lot of money.
It is really wonderful, but it is much too expensive.
I am a little sad.
I take the expensive jacket off again.
I hang it back on the clothes rail.
Then I take my green coat.
I need a warm winter coat and not a leather jacket.
